<?php require_once __DIR__ . '/db.php'; security_headers(); ?><!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>VPR Correction / Dispute</title><style>body{font-family:Arial;background:#f5f7f9;color:#17212b;margin:0}.w{max-width:850px;margin:35px auto;background:#fff;padding:32px;border-radius:12px}h1,h2{color:#062c52}p,li{line-height:1.65}.n{background:#f1f5f9;padding:14px;border-left:4px solid #062c52}a{color:#062c52}</style><?php require_once __DIR__.'/ui.php'; vpr_ui_assets(); ?></head><body><main class="w"><?php vpr_page_heading("VPR Record Correction / Dispute"); ?><p class="n">If you believe an interest recorded against a vehicle is incorrect, outdated, unauthorised or disputed, you may request a VPR review.</p><h2>What to provide</h2><ul><li>Vehicle registration number.</li><li>Your name or organisation and contact details.</li><li>VPR certificate number, if available.</li><li>A clear explanation of the disputed information.</li><li>Reasonable supporting documentation showing your connection to the vehicle or recorded interest.</li></ul><h2>Review</h2><p>VPR may contact the party associated with the recorded interest, request additional evidence, annotate or suspend a disputed entry where appropriate, and preserve an audit record of corrections.</p><h2>Submit a request</h2><p>Email <strong>info@vpr.co.zw</strong> with subject <strong>VPR RECORD REVIEW</strong>.</p><p>VPR does not adjudicate ownership or legal priority between competing parties. Matters requiring a legal determination may need to be referred to the appropriate statutory or judicial process.</p><p><a href="index.php">Return to VPR</a></p></main></body></html>